 "structural_change": "S81-TILES2 10-17 g3 (one-macro sub-beat ring): the 4-macro 1024-b bank (AQ_XMEM=1) failed gate 2 at its W/E pin walls (trial GRT overflow 502: wd_in-hi + 1,024 tied w_mask pins on the E faces, the wd-hi nets detouring round a 164-um M1-M4 wall since M5 is vertical). AQ_XMEM=2 rebuilds aq12's x wait line from the 256-b sub-beat stream: ONE 128x256 macro written every cycle with sd_, read 11 rows behind, replayed with a 3-b x 12 control line into a 1024-b re-assembly register (xr = blk delayed 12 = the flop line's xg every cycle; bit-exact bench + mutant). 1 macro at (43.2, 43.2) R0, rd/wd-lo face W toward the main std-cell band, back face (117 wd-hi + 256 ties) toward a 34.8-um E strip; outline 172.8 x 129.6 (1.33:1, was 162 x 231.12); clk on N beside the band.",
